menu "svc_listen"

    config SVC_LISTEN_CMD_REJECT_PERMILLE
        int "NVS kws/cmd_reject when the model image carries no delta1: thousandths of a nat a frame"
        range 0 65535
        default 300
        help
            The best command is turned down when the free unit loop scores better by more than this a frame
            (KEHOACH 3.12, 6.2). An image whose header carries the pair chosen for its command seeds that pair
            instead (KEHOACH 6.3). 300 is the delta1 Gate 3 was counted at (docs/measurements/command.md 2).

    config SVC_LISTEN_CMD_MARGIN_PERMILLE
        int "NVS kws/cmd_margin when the model image carries no delta2: thousandths of a nat a frame"
        range 0 65535
        default 50
        help
            The best command must lead the second by at least this a frame (KEHOACH 3.12, 6.2), unless the model
            image carries the pair chosen for its command (KEHOACH 6.3). 50 is the delta2 Gate 3 was counted at
            (docs/measurements/command.md 2).

    config SVC_LISTEN_CMD_SYLLABLE_PERMILLE
        int "NVS kws/cmd_syllable when the model image carries no delta3: thousandths of a nat a frame"
        range 1 65535
        default 65535
        help
            A command of two syllables or more is turned down when its worst syllable falls short of the free
            unit loop by more than this a frame (KEHOACH 3.12, 6.2), unless the model image carries the delta3
            chosen for its command (KEHOACH 6.3). 65535 caps nothing, as a model chosen without delta3 decides.

    config SVC_LISTEN_WAKE_PERMILLE
        int "NVS kws/wake_th when the model image carries no wake threshold: permille of the smoothed score"
        range 1 1000
        default 950
        help
            With a wake in the image, svc_listen leaves NGHE for LENH when the wake's smoothed score reaches
            this (KEHOACH 3.11, 5.4). An image whose header carries the threshold chosen for its wake seeds
            that one instead (KEHOACH 6.3).

    config SVC_LISTEN_COMMAND_WAIT_MS
        int "Milliseconds LENH waits for an utterance before going back to NGHE"
        range 100 10000
        default 3000
        help
            With a wake in the image, svc_listen goes back to NGHE when no utterance has run this long after
            the wake or after the last utterance (KEHOACH 5.4). It lives here, not in listen.yaml, whose hash
            the command model is held to.

    config SVC_LISTEN_WAKE_LEAD_MS
        int "Milliseconds of lead a command window the wake's mark cuts short is topped up to"
        range 0 2000
        default 500
        help
            In LENH a command window may not reach back past the hop after the wake's decision. When that
            leaves it less lead than this ahead of its speech, svc_listen tops the lead up with the hops right
            ahead of the wake word (KEHOACH 5.4, ADR-0032); 0 never tops up. Each topped-up hop is network
            work the decision waits for. It lives here, not in listen.yaml, whose hash the command model is
            held to.

    config SVC_LISTEN_WAKE_END_MS
        int "Milliseconds the wake's smoothed score stays over wake_th past the end of the wake word"
        range 0 1000
        default 224
        help
            In LENH the mark no command window reaches back past is the end of the wake word: the frame where
            the wake's smoothed score falls back under wake_th, less this, and never before the hop after the
            crossing (KEHOACH 5.4, ADR-0039). 224 ms is what puts the fewest marks inside "happy" on happy1's
            val_pos (docs/measurements/wake.md section 10); a new wake word or model is measured again.

    config SVC_LISTEN_WAKE_FALL_MS
        int "Milliseconds after a wake crossing its score has to fall back under wake_th to move the mark"
        range 0 5000
        default 768
        help
            A score still over wake_th this long after it crossed leaves the mark at the hop after the
            crossing, as does an utterance that closes first (KEHOACH 5.4, ADR-0039).

    config SVC_LISTEN_ENROL_WINDOW_S
        int "Seconds a speaker enrolment stays open for its commands"
        range 30 3600
        default 180
        help
            An enrolment that has not taken its commands this long after its ENROL ends, so one left behind
            neither swallows later commands nor makes anyone's voice the enrolling person's (KEHOACH 3.17).
            make speaker-enrol waits as long, then cancels.

endmenu
